Aṅguttara VIII–XI: consolidation across the collections (@buddhist-an-eights-to-elevens: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @buddhism, #source @buddhist-source-numerical-discourses, #philosophy @buddhist-dn-training-and-origination, #buddhism @buddhist-dn-training-and-origination) { r_49KP60BM2H88AGXPG75ZCRXPK9
**Read:** the books of eights through elevens in [The Numerical Discourses of the Buddha](../sources/Numerical-discourses.lingua#r_16JWQQQAWBJN7CX05AEG4WF5FR), in sequence. Complete these books rather than only reading the examples selected for a note.

Complete the collection and return to the earlier books where necessary. Consolidation concerns recalling and applying distinctions while remaining able to justify an interpretation from the text. These teachings are not doctrinally secondary because they are read late here.

**Consolidate:** Explain a selected teaching to another reader, including its assumptions and the passage supporting it. Compare an ethical application with the path and identify a limit to the application.

**Check:** show how one distinction clarifies a difficulty retained from the Saṃyutta, Majjhima, or Suttanipāta. Keep AN numbers with your examples.

**Continue:** [Dīgha: training, conditionality, and the final community](DN-Training-and-origination.lingua#r_68BHKDFQ4Y2CDWB31NXDTPEGSS).

**Return:** [Buddhism: from the path to sustained inquiry](../Buddhism.lingua#r_7P61Z6HHZNZZ8ND3DHXSFSNRRE).
